# Revision after referee reports, 2026-11-06 (appended; the entries above were made
# with the earlier impl.py, sha256 a5db1601...0f74, and are kept as a record)
# Change to impl.py: construct() raises Python's recursion limit (the recursion depth
# of solve()/k2_cut() grows linearly with the cell count; before this change a 1 x 1000
# strip raised RecursionError); docstrings updated to the final wording and symbols.
# solve() and k2_cut() are unchanged.  Python 3.15.0; all commands run from the
# supplement directory with PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1.
# sha256 of the files exercised:
#   7b51b84af773e60aac062fbe8380384a12f3b7412f071a064031833ff6af0b7d  impl.py
#   d936b4d5c07831aa4545ace720f92adeb16c9aef1b345b0c0ebc7b3a87689489  l2harness.py
#   26ccccf31fab292383925e9fda78e61f958d916cc06f1d3d78da624c39bc8d53  check_counterexample.py
#   aaecb20daeace5cf4104ea5526fb46d297526492bda4e92850f5d8ed3c99e956  check_adversarial.py
#   11e006736fa0c1e1bc45063626d7e78b4de0214c7d08d334b965f71743cbdeac  controls/C_induction_impl_v2.py
#   baba2b341f0b319492e729b5f8e43ab3464b46d7cef0edad64fe8fcd3eb36242  controls/long_strip.py
#   cd3d78cda487602e190a47b9189dc1b363ffa7b534bd1c639694e06de96635b4  controls/equiv_check.py
#   e6f2d46d5d099dc5a987c984fa5234d307c704949e79e3a4158160f423831436  controls/mutation_controls.py
#   0543af886d67ab24d822cdec15cace7e60932363b669ad52c41cdbc04eaeeb8c  controls/old_gap_example.py
#
# What the runs certify.  l2harness.py and the plain runs check only the final
# conclusions 1-4 of Lemma L2 (local feasibility, exposure, monotonicity, separation).
# The internal invariants of Lemma L2.4 (orientation in (S3), mixedness of the Step-3
# markers, the interval formulas and tie flags) are certified only by the L2DEBUG=1 runs;
# controls/mutation_controls.py shows two mutants that only L2DEBUG detects.
# Coverage notes.  Cases b1 and b2 of l2harness.py generate outward banks only, and every
# case picks at most one sub-interval per maximal run, so the random harness runs reach
# only the 'both colours' and 'unselected' clauses of (H2), never the 'meet' clause.
# Non-outward (b1)/(b2) selections, runs split into meeting banks, selections of every
# boundary halfedge, and holed polyominoes made into disks by slits are exercised by
# check_adversarial.py (and non-outward selections also by case g); the 'meet' clause
# is reached there and by the two hand-built controls of check_counterexample.py.
# The docstring of l2harness.py still labels case a "(L2(a))"; the file is a hash-pinned
# byte copy of the shared harness and is left unchanged (case a = Corollary L2a(a)).

